# yardmate-api secrets.env template
#
# COPY this file to a location OUTSIDE this repo (e.g.
# ~/.config/yardmate-api/secrets.env.prod), fill in real values, and point
# deploy.sh at it via YARDMATE_SECRETS=...
#
# NEVER commit a filled version. The repo's .gitignore covers `secrets.env`
# at any depth, but the safest habit is to keep the live copy outside the
# tree entirely.
#
# File format: see secrets/SPEC.md §2.

# ---- server config ----

# App Attest "development environment" gate. See deploy/README.md §3 for the
# stage-aware ship SOP. MUST be `false` once the App Store binary ships.
ATTEST_ALLOW_DEV=false

# ---- vended to authenticated clients ----

# OpenAI API key (GPT-4o-mini for plant chat / advice features).
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-REPLACE-ME

# Pl@ntNet API key (PRIMARY plant identification engine; Plant.id is fallback).
# Get a free key at https://my.plantnet.org (~500 req/day free tier).
PLANTNET_API_KEY=REPLACE-ME

# Plant.id API key (identification FALLBACK + sole /v1/diagnose engine).
PLANT_ID_API_KEY=REPLACE-ME

# ---- /v1/plants/enrichment (V1 plant-detail enrichment) ----

# Supabase Postgres DSN (Session Pooler form per proxy/enrichment/SPEC §9 #15).
# Get from Supabase Dashboard → Connect → Direct → "Session pooler" tab.
# Replace [YOUR-PASSWORD] with the actual DB password (use "Reset Database
# Password" in Dashboard if forgotten).
#
# DO NOT use the "Direct connection" DSN (db.<ref>.supabase.co:5432) —
# Supabase makes it IPv6-only by default and the Hetzner outbound IPv6 path
# is unreliable, which fails silently as a TCP timeout. Session Pooler is
# IPv4-routable and runs the same Postgres wire protocol so pgx connects
# identically (SPEC §9 #15).
SUPABASE_DB_URL=postgresql://postgres.REPLACE-REF:REPLACE-PASSWORD@aws-0-REPLACE-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres

# NOTE: the one-time native_region localization backfill (SPEC §7 v5) does NOT
# belong here. Its trigger ENRICH_BACKFILL_NATIVE_REGION is an OS ENV var (read
# via os.Getenv, not the vault) and MUST NOT live in this file — the long-running
# service would then run the backfill and exit on every restart. Run it as the
# dedicated one-shot `deploy/yardmate-api-backfill.service` (systemctl start
# yardmate-api-backfill) instead. It reuses SUPABASE_DB_URL + OPENAI_API_KEY above.

# ---- POST /v1/account/delete (Supabase account+data deletion + Apple revoke) ----
#
# Deletes a signed-in user's diary_entries + garden_records rows, their
# diary-images Storage objects, the Supabase auth user, AND revokes their Sign
# in with Apple grant. All SERVER-ONLY — NEVER vended to clients (not in
# main.vendedKeys), never logged.

# Supabase project base URL, e.g. https://<project-ref>.supabase.co (NO trailing
# slash). Used to reach the auth Admin API + Storage REST API.
SUPABASE_URL=https://REPLACE-REF.supabase.co

# (No SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET needed.) The client's access-token is verified against
# the project's PUBLIC JWKS (ES256) fetched from
# {SUPABASE_URL}/auth/v1/.well-known/jwks.json (Supabase asymmetric JWT signing).
# The user id (sub) is extracted from the verified token. Nothing to set here.

# Supabase service_role key (the long service_role JWT). Dashboard → Project
# Settings → API → service_role "secret". Grants RLS-bypassing admin access used
# to delete the auth user + the user's Storage objects. KEEP SECRET.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=REPLACE-ME

# ---- Sign in with Apple service account (token revoke on account deletion) ----
#
# Apple requires apps offering "Sign in with Apple" to revoke the grant when a
# user deletes their account. These mint the ES256 client_secret + call Apple's
# /auth/token + /auth/revoke. The revoke step is BEST-EFFORT (a failure is
# logged and deletion still proceeds), but ship with these set for compliance.

# Apple Developer Team ID (10 chars). Membership → Team ID. (== client_secret iss)
APPLE_TEAM_ID=PMX32RG52M

# The Sign in with Apple key's Key ID (the .p8's 10-char id). Certificates,
# Identifiers & Profiles → Keys → your key. (== client_secret JWT header `kid`)
APPLE_KEY_ID=REPLACE-ME

# App bundle id == OAuth client_id == client_secret `sub`.
APPLE_BUNDLE_ID=com.chenyao.plantapp

# The Sign in with Apple .p8 private key. TWO ways to supply it — pick ONE:
#
#   (A) APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY — the PEM contents INLINE. The secrets.env parser is
#       line-based (KEY=VALUE), so a real multi-line PEM does NOT work inline;
#       put it on ONE line with literal "\n" escapes between the PEM lines
#       (the server un-escapes "\n" back to newlines before parsing). Example:
#       APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY=-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nMIGTAg...==\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----
#
#   (B) APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH — a path to the .p8 file on the SERVER (preferred
#       for a multi-line PEM; no escaping needed). Deploy the .p8 to the host
#       yourself (e.g. /etc/yardmate-api/AuthKey_XXXXXXXXXX.p8, chmod 600, owned
#       by the yardmate-api user) and point this at it. deploy.sh does NOT ship
#       the .p8 — copy it once manually (see deploy/README.md §1).
# APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY=-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nREPLACE\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----
# APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=/etc/yardmate-api/AuthKey_REPLACE.p8

# ---- proxy/imageingest (out-of-catalog gallery ingest, v2 on-demand) ----
#
# Fills plant_images/{slug}/{1..N}.png on Cloudflare R2 via the on-demand
# iNaturalist→Wikimedia cascade, triggered by POST /v1/plants/imageingest from
# iOS. See proxy/imageingest/SPEC.md. SUPABASE_DB_URL (above) is reused for the
# plant_image_species + plant_image_files ledger tables (no plants_pending read
# in v2).
#
# Cloudflare R2 credentials — an R2 API token scoped to *Object Read & Write*
# on the yardmate-static bucket ONLY (no account-wide, no other buckets).
# SERVER-ONLY: never vended to clients (NOT in main.vendedKeys), never logged.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=REPLACE-ME
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=REPLACE-ME
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=REPLACE-ME
R2_BUCKET=yardmate-static
# R2_ENDPOINT=https://<account>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com   (optional; derived from R2_ACCOUNT_ID if unset)

# Internal manual-trigger gate for POST /internal/imageingest/run. SERVER-ONLY,
# NOT vended. The route is registered only when this is set; the request must
# carry it as the X-Ingest-Admin-Token header (constant-time compared).
IMAGEINGEST_ADMIN_TOKEN=REPLACE-ME

# Descriptive User-Agent for the iNaturalist source client (SPEC §4.1). Empty →
# built-in default UA. A missing/empty UA gets rate-clamped by iNat.
# INATURALIST_USER_AGENT=YardMate-ImageIngest/2.0 (https://yardmate.ai; contact@yardmate.ai)

# Optional v2 tuning knobs (commented = built-in defaults):
# IMAGEINGEST_USER_AGENT      Wikimedia source UA (empty → built-in default UA)
# IMAGEINGEST_PUBLIC_RATE=100 req/min per attested device for POST /v1/plants/imageingest
# IMAGEINGEST_MIN_INTERVAL=1s outbound source pacing
# IMAGEINGEST_MAX_BYTES=26214400  25 MiB download cap
#
# REMOVED in v2 (no longer read): IMAGEINGEST_TICK_INTERVAL (ticker removed),
# IMAGEINGEST_BATCH_LIMIT (batch-from-seed removed).

# Codex #22 release-coordination gate. Keep false until the iOS Settings →
# Credits page (which renders credits.json) is LIVE: while false, only CC0 /
# Public-domain images are uploaded (no attribution required → compliant);
# CC-BY / CC-BY-SA candidates are recorded deferred_attribution and uploaded
# only after this flips true. Flipping it ON before the Credits page exists
# would serve attribution-required images with no visible credit (a license
# violation). NOT a permanent BY/SA-off switch — it re-processes deferred rows.
IMAGEINGEST_ALLOW_ATTRIBUTION_LICENSES=false

# --- /v1/feedback operator email (all three FROM/PASS/TO required to enable;
# any missing = mail disabled, feedback rows still stored in Supabase) ---
# Same Gmail app-password account as the yardmate-onfail systemd alert, but
# read from this vault (the alert's /etc/yardmate-alert/smtp-pass is root-only
# and the API runs as the yardmate-api user).
# FEEDBACK_SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com   (default when unset)
# FEEDBACK_SMTP_PORT=587              (default when unset)
# FEEDBACK_SMTP_FROM=<gmail address the app password belongs to>
# FEEDBACK_SMTP_PASS=<gmail app password>
# FEEDBACK_EMAIL_TO=<operator inbox that receives each feedback message>

# --- catalog name-index hot-load (proxy/SPEC.md §9) ---
# OFF by default (kill-switch). When true, a background poller conditional-GETs
# the CDN plants_index.json (ETag version gate) and atomically swaps identify's
# name→id lookup maps with ZERO downtime, so a freshly catalog-promoted plant is
# recognised by /v1/identify within one poll interval WITHOUT a redeploy. Fail-
# safe: the embedded plants_index is always the cold-start baseline and any poll/
# parse error keeps the last good table (a truncated/half-published object is
# refused). Only the plants_index-derived name maps hot-load; plants_detail.json
# + diseases.json stay embed-only. Roll back = set false + restart.
# Validate on staging first (point URL at content-staging/, interval 1m).
# CATALOG_HOTLOAD_ENABLED=false
# CATALOG_HOTLOAD_URL=https://images.yardmate.ai/content/plants_index.json
# CATALOG_HOTLOAD_INTERVAL=10m    (any Go duration; floored at 1m)

# --- /v1/doctor conversational diagnosis (doctor/SPEC.md) ---
# Streams structured plant-doctor replies over SSE. Needs OPENAI_API_KEY
# (shared with enrichment/vision above); key absent = route unregistered.
# DOCTOR_ENABLED: master switch, DEFAULT OFF. Deploying the binary must not
# open a new paid surface by itself (prod already carries OPENAI_API_KEY, so
# without this gate any routine deploy would put /v1/doctor live before the
# app update ships). staging: set true to validate; prod: flip when the iOS
# release is ready.
# DOCTOR_MODEL: whitelist gpt-4o-mini | gpt-4o | gpt-5-mini | gpt-5;
# anything else falls back to gpt-4o-mini with a WARN at boot.
# DOCTOR_ALLOW_MODEL_OVERRIDE: dev/staging ONLY. When true, a client-sent
# `model` field (still whitelist-bound) wins over DOCTOR_MODEL — this is how
# the iOS debug screen switches models. Prod stays false: overrides are then
# silently ignored, so a leaked/stale debug build cannot pick the dear model.
# DOCTOR_HOURLY_BUDGET: the endpoint's own hourly call ceiling (separate from
# the identify/diagnose budget — neither traffic class may starve the other).
# DOCTOR_ENABLED=false
# DOCTOR_MODEL=gpt-5
# DOCTOR_FOLLOWUP_MODEL=gpt-5-mini   # 第 DOCTOR_LEAD_TURNS+1 轮起的省钱档；不设=全程 DOCTOR_MODEL
# DOCTOR_LEAD_TURNS=2
# XAI_API_KEY=xai-...   # 配了才有 grok-* 可选；缺省 grok 选择自动回落默认模型
# DOCTOR_ALLOW_MODEL_OVERRIDE=false
# DOCTOR_HOURLY_BUDGET=200

# --- Plantdex rarity pipeline (proxy/rarity/SPEC.md) ---
# Two independent switches, both DEFAULT OFF (deploying the binary must not
# start writing counters or publishing CDN objects by itself):
#
# RARITY_COUNT_ENABLED: best-effort per-species counter write on /v1/identify
# success (dex_identify_daily, migration 012 — apply the SQL first). Failure
# never affects the identify response. Flip on staging first, then prod (data
# accrues from that moment; there is no backfill by design).
# RARITY_PUBLISH_ENABLED: periodic aggregate → {RARITY_R2_PREFIX}/dex/rarity.json
# publish on the shared R2 bucket (reuses the imageingest R2_* creds above).
# flags.json-style: does NOT touch version.txt (its single writer stays
# catalog-promote-tool/deploy_shards.sh).
#
# RARITY_R2_PREFIX: "content" (prod default) | "content-staging" (staging MUST
# set this — the bucket is shared and prefix routing is the only isolation).
# RARITY_MIN_SAMPLE: species below this all-time scan count are omitted from
# the artifact (cold-start gate; the iOS Plantdex hides rarity for absent ids).
# RARITY_MIN_SPECIES: below this many eligible species the species map
# publishes empty — with only head species eligible, percentile tiers would
# brand the least common of them "legendary". Hide beats mislabel.
# RARITY_TIER_CUTS: ascending species-percentile boundaries for
# common/uncommon/rare/very-rare/legendary. Malformed → WARN + defaults.
# RARITY_PUBLISH_INTERVAL: publish cadence (Go duration; floored at 10m).
# RARITY_ADMIN_TOKEN: gates POST /internal/rarity/rebuild (manual trigger for
# staging verification; served only on localhost — nginx 404s non-/v1 paths).
# SERVER-ONLY, never vended; route unregistered when unset.
# RARITY_COUNT_ENABLED=false
# RARITY_PUBLISH_ENABLED=false
# RARITY_R2_PREFIX=content
# RARITY_MIN_SAMPLE=50
# RARITY_MIN_SPECIES=100
# RARITY_TIER_CUTS=0.40,0.70,0.85,0.95
# RARITY_PUBLISH_INTERVAL=24h
# RARITY_ADMIN_TOKEN=REPLACE-ME
